5) the mechanics are the ones the copy describes
   wall at its widest: Through the wall and in. (open 1.00); the same shot half a cycle later: Into the wall. It was shut. (open 0.00)
   on the loose ball: Ball won. He pushed it too far and you read it.; on the man: You took the man. Free kick, and a word from the ref.; on the ball at his feet: Ball was at his feet. Straight through him, foul.; wide: Nowhere near it. He is past you.
   full stretch (1.00) leaving in time: Full stretch. Kept it out.; leaving at less than half the dive: Nowhere near. In the net.
6) growth is bounded and respects headroom: at most +2, never past the ceiling, once a season
   70 with an 80 ceiling: 8 of 10 pays +2, 5 of 10 pays +1, 4 of 10 pays 0; 79 pays at most +1; at or past 80 pays 0
   2500 overall and ceiling pairs times three scores: 0 paid past the ceiling or past +2
   once a season, only the drill's attribute, and a skilled run averages 6.8, 8.1, 8.4 wins against the 5 that pays

simCareerDrills: green. The gap has to be timed, the ball has to be loose, the corner has to be left for early, and nobody grows past his ceiling.
